WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.352
A complete Vim

00:00:01.164 --> 00:00:01.894
manual

00:00:01.942 --> 00:00:03.015
written over four

00:00:02.826 --> 00:00:03.628
years

00:00:04.158 --> 00:00:05.242
The author spent

00:00:05.078 --> 00:00:06.209
almost a decade

00:00:06.021 --> 00:00:06.905
playing with Vim

00:00:07.118 --> 00:00:07.872
and after a

00:00:07.684 --> 00:00:08.674
couple of hours

00:00:08.486 --> 00:00:09.299
he could write

00:00:09.182 --> 00:00:10.349
and edit content

00:00:10.502 --> 00:00:11.846
more productively and

00:00:11.658 --> 00:00:12.695
with more fun

00:00:13.222 --> 00:00:13.953
The book is

00:00:13.764 --> 00:00:15.191
a step-by-step approach

00:00:15.003 --> 00:00:15.934
with no less

00:00:15.746 --> 00:00:16.854
than one hundred

00:00:16.665 --> 00:00:18.257
seventy fun exercises

00:00:18.069 --> 00:00:19.023
to build muscle

00:00:18.835 --> 00:00:19.448
memory

00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:20.981
chapter by chapter

00:00:21.518 --> 00:00:22.272
It is aimed

00:00:22.084 --> 00:00:23.416
at real-life examples

00:00:23.334 --> 00:00:23.970
with a rich

00:00:23.782 --> 00:00:24.477
annexe as a

00:00:24.289 --> 00:00:24.996
reference

00:00:25.138 --> 00:00:25.928
and the author

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:27.166
says even long-time

00:00:26.978 --> 00:00:27.944
Vim users will

00:00:27.756 --> 00:00:28.676
learn something

00:00:29.214 --> 00:00:30.228
Full story on

00:00:30.039 --> 00:00:30.935
the dashboard
